+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Why CVE-2025-69650 Is a False Positive for **binutils 2.45.1** on Alpine 3.23
+
+## Overview: What Is **binutils**?
+
+**binutils** is a collection of binary tools used in software development. It includes
+utilities like `as` (assembler), `ld` (linker), `objdump`, `readelf`, `nm`, and others.
+Alpine 3.23 ships GNU Binutils **2.45.1** (`pkgver=2.45.1`, package `2.45.1-r0`).
+
+## Why This Vulnerability Does Not Affect 2.45.1
+
+Security scanners may flag CVE-2025-69650 against `binutils` even when:
+
+- The vulnerable subsystem (`all_relocations` / `--got-contents` support in `readelf`)
+  was introduced on git master **after** the `binutils-2_45_1` release tag
+- Alpine 3.23 ships the tagged release **2.45.1**, which never contained the vulnerable code
+- MITRE/NVD mark the CVE as **DISPUTED**: the double-free only reproduced in pre-release
+  git-master code and did not affect any tagged Binutils release
+
+These factors cause scanners to **misidentify this CVE as present**, leading to a
+**false positive** for Alpine 3.23.
+
+---
+## 📌 CVE-2025-69650 – False Positive in binutils 2.45.1
+
+**Component:** `dump_relocations` / `process_got_section_contents` in `binutils/readelf.c`
+**Issue:** Early return before initializing `all_relocations[]`, so an uninitialized
+`r_symbol` pointer may be passed to `free()` (CWE-415 double free / DoS via SIGABRT)
+**Impact:** Denial of service in `readelf` when processing a crafted ELF — **only** on
+pre-release code that included the `--got-contents` feature
+
+---
+
+## 🔍 Vulnerability Overview
+
+- **Vulnerable feature introduced by:** commit `81e90cf63a10ad11772c2437c8f2a88f1a00c739`
+  (`--got-contents` / `all_relocations` state) on git master after `binutils-2_45_1`
+- **Upstream fix:** commit `ea4bc025abdba85a90e26e13f551c16a44bfa921`
+  (zero `all_relocations` in `update_all_relocations`)
+- **Severity (reported):** High (CVSS 7.5) — disputed for tagged releases
+- **Attack vector:** Local/crafted ELF via `readelf` (DoS only; no RCE observed)
+
+---
+
+## ✅ binutils 2.45.1 (Alpine 3.23) – Why This Is a False Positive
+
+- Alpine 3.23 package version: **2.45.1-r0** (`applicable_version`: `2.45.1`)
+- Independent source inspection of tag `binutils-2_45_1` / tarball `binutils-2.45.1`
+  shows **zero** occurrences of:
+  - `all_relocations`
+  - `update_all_relocations`
+  - `process_got_section_contents`
+  - `OPTION_GOT_CONTENTS`
+  in `binutils/readelf.c`
+- Because the vulnerable subsystem is absent, applying the upstream fix commit would be
+  a no-op / would not apply — there is nothing to backport
+- CVE status: **DISPUTED** (behavior only in pre-release git-master; not in tagged releases)
+
+---
+
+## ⚠️ Why You Don't Need a Code Fix
+
+- **No vulnerable code present in 2.45.1**
+- **No security impact** on Alpine 3.23 systems shipping this package
+- Scanner alerts are **false positives** from version-range matching without code validation
+- This `dummy.patch` records the not-affected determination for Root.io's patch metadata
+
+---
+
+## 🔗 References
+
+- [NVD – CVE-2025-69650](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-69650)
+- [Alpine Security Tracker – CVE-2025-69650](https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2025-69650)
+- [Alpine package – binutils 3.23](https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/package/v3.23/main/x86_64/binutils)
+- [Upstream fix – ea4bc025abdb](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=binutils-gdb.git;a=commit;h=ea4bc025abdba85a90e26e13f551c16a44bfa921)
+- [Feature intro – 81e90cf63a10](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=binutils-gdb.git;a=commit;h=81e90cf63a10ad11772c2437c8f2a88f1a00c739)
+
